  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "The graph shows f(x) tending to 3 as x tends to negative infinity. Thus 1/f(x) tends to the positive value 1/3, while x² grows without bound, so x²/f(x) tends to positive infinity. This confirms the earlier answer and matches MA's worked solution, which reduces the requested limit to that of x²/3. The exact current choice is option 1.",
